,"received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williamjblair/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #4816.\n\nConjecture 5 of [Fradelizi, Manui, Meyer, Ndiaye](https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.03582): among planar convex bodies with a centre of symmetry containing the origin, equality in Corollary 29 holds only for parallelograms with a vertex at the origin. Corollary 29 and its sharpness case are here too, since the conjecture is about when that bound is attained.\n\n### Two definitions Mathlib does not have\n\n**The Firey `L_p`-sum.** The source defines `K ⊕ₚ L` by its support function, `h = (h_K^p + h_L^p)^(1/p)` (equation 4), which needs an argument that such a body exists. Here it is the intersection of the halfspaces that support function cuts out:\n\n```lean\nnoncomputable def lpSum (p : ℝ) (K L : Set E) : Set E :=\n  {x | ∀ u : E, inner ℝ x u ≤ (supportFunction K u ^ p + supportFunction L u ^ p) ^ (1 / p)}\n```\n\nSame set on the bodies these statements quantify over, and no existence argument needed.\n\n**The support function** itself, as `⨆ x : K, ⟪x, u⟫`. Mathlib has `ConvexBody` and `gauge` but nothing for this.\n\n### Checks\n\n`rsConstant_two` is proved rather than `sorry`d: at `p = q = 2` the constant is `Γ(3/2)²/Γ(2) · 2 + 2 = π/2 + 2`. It pins down that `rsConstant` is the right expression, which is the part of the statement easiest to get wrong. `#print axioms` gives the standard three, and the value agrees numerically to 10 decimal places.\n\nThe conjecture text and the Corollary 29 constant are quoted from the PDF rather than the issue.","labels":[{"id":8685751703,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOogmB88AAAACBbYNlw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google-deepmind/formal-conjectures/labels/arxiv","name":"arxiv","description":"","color":"ffffff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":8733797982,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOogmB88AAAACCJMuXg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google-deepmind/fo